{"t":1786195222709,"type":"FeatureCollection","features":[{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0946e973447564aed476f655e9cded488110f7f7.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-150.88,62.01],[-150.67,61.86],[-150.8,61.77],[-151.15,61.92],[-151.08,61.99],[-150.88,62.01]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0946e973447564aed476f655e9cded488110f7f7.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0946e973447564aed476f655e9cded488110f7f7.001.1","areaDesc":"Western Susitna Valley","geocode":{"SAME":["002170"],"UGC":["AKZ745"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/forecast/AKZ745"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c4f2259a84ad44e4728e395ff49d445ac176fe71.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c4f2259a84ad44e4728e395ff49d445ac176fe71.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-08-04T08:14:00-08:00"},{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.06a3dc8a6faacbf0430ab2e127360ea830dbc45d.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.06a3dc8a6faacbf0430ab2e127360ea830dbc45d.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-08-04T15:54:00-08:00"},{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f3467287ef79dc049006dae219bbf88d0bc21e17.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f3467287ef79dc049006dae219bbf88d0bc21e17.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-08-05T04:18:00-08:00"},{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.52281d77d9ac4a142cf9a7b4098ae232b4a36f3e.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.52281d77d9ac4a142cf9a7b4098ae232b4a36f3e.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-08-05T13:54:00-08:00"}],"sent":"2026-08-07T11:00:00-08:00","effective":"2026-08-07T11:00:00-08:00","onset":"2026-08-07T11:00:00-08:00","expires":"2026-08-08T13:00:00-08:00","ends":"2026-08-08T13:00:00-08:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Likely","urgency":"Expected","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Anchorage AK","headline":"Flood Warning issued August 7 at 11:00AM AKDT until August 8 at 1:00PM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.\n\n* WHERE...Yentna River including Lake Creek.\n\n* WHEN...Until 100 PM AKDT Saturday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1053 AM AKDT, the river remains in moderate flood stage\nafter heavy rains earlier this week, but is beginning to\nsubside. The river crested at 22.52 ft around 8pm Thursday,\nAugust 7th.\n- For Yentna River at Lake Creek:\nAt 9:50am the stage was 22.3 feet.\nFlood Stage is 20.5 feet.\n\nImpacts:\nAt 20.5 feet: Anglers Inn & King Point Lodges will have water\nin several cabins.\n\n\n\nAt 22.0 feet: McDougal's, King Point, Anglers Inn, Wilderness\nPlace, Lake Creek Lodge, 3-Rivers, and Cottonwood Resorts\nwill have water in a number of cabins with water also\nencroaching the main lodge buildings.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Stay tuned to further developments by listening to your local radio,\ntelevision, or NOAA Weather Radio for further information.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLWAFC"],"WMOidentifier":["WGAK48 PAFC 071900"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING NOW IN EFFECT UNTIL 1 PM AKDT SATURDAY"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.EXT.PAFC.FA.W.0005.000000T0000Z-260808T2100Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-08T13:00:00-08:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["FLW"],"NationalWeatherService":["FAW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4012e8981516f4acc66aaf3deb0be40ca8d1a929.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-98.8,28.17],[-98.59,28.36],[-98.33,28.45],[-98.33,28.33],[-98.54,28.26],[-98.8,28.07],[-98.8,28.17]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4012e8981516f4acc66aaf3deb0be40ca8d1a929.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4012e8981516f4acc66aaf3deb0be40ca8d1a929.001.1","areaDesc":"McMullen, TX","geocode":{"SAME":["048311"],"UGC":["TXC311"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/TXC311"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a4006eb38dda81396de878a3ee30877db05dc184.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a4006eb38dda81396de878a3ee30877db05dc184.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-08-07T08:43:00-05:00"}],"sent":"2026-08-07T20:14:00-05:00","effective":"2026-08-07T20:14:00-05:00","onset":"2026-08-07T20:14:00-05:00","expires":"2026-08-08T11:15:00-05:00","ends":"2026-08-08T21:48:00-05:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Corpus Christi TX","headline":"Flood Warning issued August 7 at 8:14PM CDT until August 8 at 9:48PM CDT by NWS Corpus Christi TX","description":"...The Flood Warning is extended for the following rivers in Texas...\n\nNueces River Near Tilden affecting McMullen County.\n\nFor the Nueces River...including Tilden...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise to a crest of 15.2 feet\njust after midnight tonight. It will then fall below flood stage\nlate tonight.\n- Flood stage is 14.0 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 15.2\nfeet on 09/19/1983.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nMotorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nEven 6 inches of fast-moving flood water can knock you off your feet\nand a depth of 2 feet will float your car. Never try to walk, swim,\nor drive through such swift water. If you come upon flood waters,\nstop, turn around and go another way.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov/crp.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSCRP"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS84 KCRP 080114"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.EXT.KCRP.FL.W.0026.000000T0000Z-260809T0248Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-08T21:48:00-05:00"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.422f915b9c8698a61ceeecbb773519636c1559f0.001.1,2026-08-06T20:04:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6c086fb0cb122a2dcaad2d633e16163ca1e2f740.002.1,2026-08-06T08:31:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cd351168adba7b138d4b2fd5b257e34ba80d69c4.002.1,2026-08-05T19:53:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.15a54361c4ea7596611f53154fbe235d68afe15a.002.1,2026-08-05T10:56:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cfe0cb53516243e5682c1b93f097af5f347ba9d1.002.1,2026-08-04T20:07:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0d85f3f3b48cc9017f55a16e1f1acf4cc74e9f0b.002.1,2026-08-04T15:51:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.52c53adf21b8a3c6773f1bc49de7351006f6e777.002.1,2026-08-04T08:54:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1890e16dec93bc7bd2c40c556f7d88b51dfba240.002.1,2026-08-03T20:13:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6c2d46f696ba508a8268a87165a57be61f4e50bb.002.1,2026-08-03T09:17:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a89341f8395f18ac2219ce1a412989c19cd5d270.002.1,2026-08-02T20:24:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.135a0f1988967bd17c986e8c8d19aa89231c27b7.002.1,20